			<div class="content" id="post-content-4821291">
									

<p>It's making progress, but there is still a lot that needs to be looked at.<br />
Initial thoughts: I love the addition of decoding a message, it adds to the mysterious aspect of this scp. The narrative could be what makes or breaks this scp though, and in it's current state is breaking it a bit.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;How&nbsp;so?</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Ahh,&nbsp;I&nbsp;see.</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>The Stone's discovery has an interesting warrant, but it's kinda anti climatic to say that he just 'found it', you know what I mean? For now, I would scrap the recovery, as it stands it only really takes up word count.</p>
<p>The researcher also suddenly discovering it's anomolous properties doesn't really make sense, and for the following reasons:<br />
Number 1, unless it had some other characteristic that made it worth containment, it wouldn't have ended up with the foundation in the first place if they didn't know that it did this; Number 2, the researcher wouldn't bother to see if an scp was in good condition if it was so unproblematic that it was forgotten about. Why contain it even?<br />
Rather than resolving these issues, I would suggest instead you scrap them, and using a different approach.</p>
<p>Now: by itself, I think making this a numbered scp is going to be a very uphill climb. It has the weird bit down, and I think it speaking opens up possibilities for a lot of creep factor in the future, but the narrative is tough.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>My prescription? I would take a break from the narrative for a bit and focus on something else.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;One&nbsp;interesting&nbsp;path&nbsp;forward&nbsp;may&nbsp;be&nbsp;found&nbsp;with&nbsp;the&nbsp;introduction&nbsp;of&nbsp;SCP-XXXX-2.</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Hide</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Let's say that SCP-XXXX-1 is The Stone and SCP-XXXX-2 is this larger entity you've had on the backburner for a while now (this would be the proper numeration if you did a -1 -2 etc). In another reply you mention tentacles/arms surging up from the earth (<em>I like the visual</em>), I'm reminded of cthulu type-monsters, it's buried beneath the earth, buried things are old; In my mind, buried + hugetentaclearms.jpg = a &quot;this thing's older than humanity&quot; type-beat.</p>
<p>The original idea establishes that the stone predicts natural disasters, and in the updated version you added the concept that this Stone can relay messages, which have coordinates and then a word. Take what you have, and use it establish <strong>motivation.</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>You said that the stone was a part of SCP-XXXX-2, is it a messenger of some kind? What kind of words does it say? Has the entirety of the message been decoded?</li>
<li>The stone tells us that a natural disaster is coming. How does it know? Did it cause the disaster? What does the Stone communicate about this larger entity's motives? Is it hostile, and if so why would it choose to send us coordinates of the disaster and a voicemail?</li>
<li>The Foundation gives a heads up to Puerto Rico, acting as a sort of early warning system, ensuring that less people die. Was this the intention of SCP-XXXX-2? How would this entity react if the Foundation decided to keep doing this? Would it react right away?</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>If you can properly establish the motivation of these different parties, then we can move on to what actually happens narratively. I hope that my thoughts help you as you build more this story!</p>
<p>If anything I said is confusing, feel free to pm me</p>

							</div>

								
					
