				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/cybersqyd" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5336470); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5336470&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1605837974" alt="cybersqyd" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5336470)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/cybersqyd" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5336470); return false;" >cybersqyd</a></span> <span class="odate time_1605620875 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">17 Nov 2020 13:47</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4820795">
									

<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[+]&nbsp;Open&nbsp;for&nbsp;crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-XXXX changes color from Onyx Black (#0f0f0f) to Alizarin Crimson (#e32636) 1 month before natural disaster or pandemics. The total duration of the color change predicts the death tool of the disaster.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>How does this prediction work if it always changes colour a month before the natural disaster/pandemic? Like it seems to me that it'd be based on the length of time <em>after</em> the disaster which in turn doesn't feel like a prediction?</p>
<p>Beyond this, surely it'd be Alizarin Crimson basically all the time since the world is constantly experiencing disease outbreaks and minor natural disasters and flooding?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>It only possesses 30% of magnetite and does not possess ferromagnetic metals such as nickel or iron.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>magnetite is an iron oxide and so it would contain iron</p>
<p>Beyond these relatively minor technical concerns, my biggest concern is 'so what?'. Like, <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/grigori-karpin" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4558017); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4558017&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1605620875" alt="Grigori Karpin" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4558017)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/grigori-karpin" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4558017); return false;">Grigori Karpin</a></span> kinda touched on this but your central narrative is very focussed on -1 without really any indication of:</p>
<ul>
<li>how the foundation figures out it exists/that it's the centre of the earth</li>
<li>what it being the centre of earth actually like. means in real world terms?</li>
<li>why scp-xxxx was so close to the crust of the planet if the thing is at the centre of the world</li>
</ul>
<p>Even with these though, it really needs like&#8230;an actual story to be told about this thing? Some kinda exploration of why it's existence is both interesting and affects people (likely the Foundation) in some manner. Maybe this is related to its effects and the Foundation trying to decide whether they can like, figure out where the natural disasters will be and help folk without revealing themselves say, or perhaps some kind narrative where you quietly end up implying the existence of -1 and, in turn, some kind of implication as a result.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

							</div>

								
					
